  "note": "the trade off is close to one for one and the rules sit at different points on it rather than at different qualities. The z score rule destroys the least and catches a third of the errors; the rolling interquartile rule catches three quarters and destroys three quarters. Under the two rules that catch most of the errors, the large majority of what is removed is real demand. That is not a tuning failure: a promotion and a mis keyed quantity are the same shape and a rule that sees only the series cannot separate them",
